Q6. Indian mobile number consists of 10 digits. The first four digits from the left represent the area code while the next 6 digits represent the extension. For example, 9910235674 is a valid mobile number, where 9910 represent the area code, while 235674 represent the extension. A file called MobileNumberRecord contains 100 such mobile numbers written using the following structure:
```c
struct MobileNo
{
    int area;
    int extension;
};
```

Write a C program that will create a new file called Filtered that stores all those mobile numbers which are divisible by the sum of digits of its area code.
For example, 8034125730 is divisible by the sum of digits of its area code (8+0+3+4=15)


